# Accepted govulncheck advisories — reachable findings that CANNOT be fixed by
# bumping a dependency. Every entry needs a reason and an exit condition,
# exactly like carried pins (docs/guides/DEPENDENCIES.md §Carrying local
# patches), and the whole file is re-audited on every T2 upgrade.
#
# Adding an entry here is a last resort: if a fixed release exists, bump the
# module instead (T0 runbook). `make deps-verify` fails on any reachable
# advisory not listed here.

# golang.org/x/crypto/openpgp is unmaintained BY DESIGN — the advisory is
# permanent and no fixed version will ever exist (we are on the latest
# x/crypto). Reached via cosmos-sdk x/upgrade → hashicorp/go-getter, whose
# GPG-verification path timeflare never invokes (upgrade artefacts are not
# fetched with detached-signature checksums). Exit: when go-getter replaces
# openpgp (hashicorp/go-getter#solved upstream) or x/upgrade drops go-getter —
# re-check on every T2 upgrade.
